WEBVTT - SWID-SHRK Aerospace & Mechanics Laboratory
Title: Plate Antiprism Modeling — Part 2
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00.000 --> 00:08.000
<v Dr. Pouria Hejazi>Welcome to Part 2 of Plate Antiprism Modeling: S4R shell meshing, self-contact interaction penalty, and energy absorption evaluation.

2
00:08.000 --> 00:22.000
<v Dr. Pouria Hejazi>Discretize the folded facets using S4R 4-node doubly curved shell elements with reduced integration and finite membrane strain formulation.

3
00:22.000 --> 00:38.000
<v Dr. Pouria Hejazi>Configure Abaqus/Explicit General Contact with penalty tangential friction mu = 0.20 to model facet-on-facet contact as the cellular origami folds and compacts.

4
00:38.000 --> 00:54.000
<v Dr. Pouria Hejazi>Set up dynamic explicit crush loading with a prescribed rigid plate velocity of 10.0 m/s and extract reaction force and internal energy dissipation (ALLIE).

5
00:54.000 --> 01:10.000
<v Dr. Pouria Hejazi>Analyze the crushing curve to compute the Crush Force Efficiency (CFE = F_mean / F_peak). The origami fold design provides an exceptionally stable plateau without force spikes.
